# The secrets of polestar. Copy this file to .env and fill in the values there.
# Git ignores .env but keeps this file, so never write values here.
#
# `cf dev` reads .env, and `cf deploy --secrets-file .env` uploads it with the Worker.

# ANALYTICS_API_TOKEN
#   A Cloudflare API token that reads the usage of the account that polestar watches.
#   It belongs to the account rather than to a person, and it can only read.
#
#   To issue it:
#   1. Open this link. It opens the form for a new account API token, with the
#      name "polestar" and two permissions selected: Account Analytics Read and D1 Read.
#      https://dash.cloudflare.com/?to=/:account/api-tokens&permissionGroupKeys=%5B%7B%22key%22%3A%22account_analytics%22%2C%22type%22%3A%22read%22%7D%2C%7B%22key%22%3A%22d1%22%2C%22type%22%3A%22read%22%7D%5D&name=polestar
#   2. If Cloudflare asks for an account, choose the account that polestar watches.
#   3. Keep the two permissions and add no other. Select "Continue to summary",
#      then "Create Token".
#   4. Copy the token, which Cloudflare shows only once, and paste it after
#      ANALYTICS_API_TOKEN= below.
#
#   To replace it, issue a new token the same way, paste it here, deploy again,
#   and delete the old token on the Account API Tokens page of the account.
ANALYTICS_API_TOKEN=
